    {
      "id": "injury-report-s1-w19",
      "type": "feature",
      "author": "tessa-wren",
      "title": "Smoth’s five-week absence changes Saffron’s divisional preparation",
      "dek": "Three new positive-week injuries are confirmed after the wild-card round; Mt. Silver’s bye clears one counter while several major absences continue.",
      "teams": [],
      "body": [
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Saffron has the most consequential new absence among the remaining eight teams. Emmitt Smoth is listed for five weeks after the Olivine game. He carried twice for fourteen yards in the 42–10 win. Dam Skattebo supplied the larger rushing workload, with ninety-four yards and two touchdowns, so the immediate task is to preserve that production while accounting for the missing backfield option. No replacement workload has been announced in the evidence reviewed here."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The other new positive-week injuries belong to eliminated teams: Olivine’s Magmar is listed for four weeks and Hearthome’s Palafin for two. Their entries remain part of the league-wide report even though they no longer affect a divisional matchup. The table distinguishes these new injuries from ordinary one-week reductions on older recovery counters."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Mt. Silver’s bye brought Ninji Asomugha’s counter to zero. Tic Thorpe still has two weeks reported, Josh Alakazam three, Tony Gyarzalez four and Vibrava four. Ariados remains at nine and Medicham at three. The Reds face Hatterene’s Blackthorn passing game with several continuing absences; a cleared counter for Asomugha does not establish the exact defensive lineup."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Blackthorn’s Exploud also reached zero, while Sawsbuck remains at three weeks. Lavender’s Mr. Clanky remains at four. Mossdeep’s Poury Holt remains at five, Sunyshore’s 88 Special at fifteen, and Petalburg’s Oinkologne at one. The last of those is particularly relevant to a game against Sunyshore’s productive rushing attack: the Pride’s available backfield just won with Glalie and Whiscash, while its 957-yard regular-season runner still carries a positive counter."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Several important players received new minor entries with zero remaining weeks, including Saffron’s HeeDee Lamb and Pach Tatum, Sunyshore’s Serp Gardener, Nair Jordan and BJ Vickers, and Petalburg’s Glalie. These entries do not support an invented missed game or a questionable designation. Dewford’s Dusclops and Lavender’s Vikavolt and Axew are in the same zero-week category."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Reported weeks describe the current injury record. A reduction is recovery progress, not a newly suffered injury. A cleared designation establishes neither an appearance nor a starting role, and a healthy player still on injured reserve requires an actual roster move before that status changes. Game reports do not supply reliable injury timestamps, so this report does not assign an injury to a particular play."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "The comparison below covers every player with an injury entry in either this issue or the preceding issue. Regular-season and wild-card evidence remain separate; the table reports current availability changes rather than estimating medical return dates."
        },
